paperweight-secrets (0.1.3-1) trixie; urgency=low

  * Ship ~/.gtkrc-2.0 skel default: Catppuccin Macchiato dark colors for
    pinentry-gtk2 (and any other GTK2 app), via direct style overrides —
    no theme engine, same hardcoded-per-theme convention already used for
    gtklock/wofi/waybar. GTK2 has no GTK3+-style "prefer-dark" toggle, so
    this is the whole mechanism. Static to Macchiato, doesn't track live
    theme switching.

 -- Alex Long <johnalexanderlong@gmail.com>  Thu, 16 Jul 2026 17:00:00 -0500

paperweight-secrets (0.1.2-1) trixie; urgency=high

  * Fix gpg-agent.conf pointing pinentry-program at /usr/bin/pinentry-gtk2
    (found during live testing: "No pinentry" on any operation needing the
    secret key). The pinentry-gtk2 *package* installs its binary at
    /usr/bin/pinentry-gtk-2 (hyphenated) — never verified against the real
    installed path, just assumed it matched the package name. Fixed in
    both the skel gpg-agent.conf default and paperweight-secrets-init's
    merge logic. Existing installs need a manual one-line sed fix to
    ~/.gnupg/gpg-agent.conf; re-running paperweight-secrets-init won't
    correct an already-present (wrong) directive.

 -- Alex Long <johnalexanderlong@gmail.com>  Thu, 16 Jul 2026 16:00:00 -0500

paperweight-secrets (0.1.1-1) trixie; urgency=high

  * Fix $mod+p doing nothing on existing-user installs (found during live
    testing): postinst propagated the new bashrc.d fragment to an
    already-existing user's home directory but never the sway keybind
    fragment (60-secrets-keys.conf) — /etc/skel only reaches brand-new
    accounts via adduser. Now propagated the same way as the bashrc.d
    fragment.

 -- Alex Long <johnalexanderlong@gmail.com>  Thu, 16 Jul 2026 14:00:00 -0500

paperweight-secrets (0.1.0-1) trixie; urgency=low

  * Initial packaging. Distro-wide secrets manager: pass + pam-gnupg +
    pass-secret-service. Patches /etc/pam.d/greetd and /etc/pam.d/gtklock
    to preset the gpg-agent passphrase cache at login and screen-unlock.
    Ships gpg-agent.conf skel default, a $mod+p passmenu wofi picker, and
    paperweight-secrets-init(1) for guided first-time setup.
  * Add paperweight-secrets-sync: mirrors CLI pass(1) entries into
    pass-secret-service's store as symlinks (readable Label via a synthesized
    .properties sidecar) so libsecret apps can see them too; prunes stale
    mirrors and best-effort restarts the D-Bus service to pick up changes.
    paperweight-passmenu updated to show D-Bus-created secrets by their
    Label instead of their raw id — the two directions of the CLI/app
    bridge, verified end-to-end against a real pass-secret-service instance.

 -- Alex Long <johnalexanderlong@gmail.com>  Thu, 16 Jul 2026 09:00:00 -0500
